<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lakhdhirji Waghji</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1876–1957</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Lakhdhirji</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lakhdhirji Waghji was the Thakore Sahib, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a>, of Morvi in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Kathiawar</a> from 1922 until the state joined the United State of Saurashtra in 1948. He continued his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waghji-ii">Waghji II</a>'s development of railways, the port of Navlakhi and local industry, making Morbi a centre of manufacturing, and endowed institutions such as the engineering college in Morbi that bears his name.</p></div>
